Z||000000||wwh0001||10-11-2000||03:53 PM||||i am having a problem with my ac/heater controls. ( 88 Formula) When i change from heat to ac or defrost the air duct levers do not always changed the flow of air. If the heat has be turned on and the air is flowing out the bottom the air will somtimes not switch to the dash vents when a/c is turned on. (Your feet get very cold.) I know there are a couple of motors that control this. When you hear the motors turning the air flow will change to where it should be. However somtimes these motors do not come on and change the flow.( usually when it is cold).Is there a relay for these motors ? Motors burning out ? Anyone have any ideas ? Thanks. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-11-2000||04:25 PM||||The problem is likely the controls in your case. Try another set of them. Check the plugs are clean and tight.<P>The controls are easier to get to than the motors. you have to take out the radio to get to one of them. the other is way up under the dash.||||reg||1
